# fuzz-rv32-jit's dictionary: the instructions that reach the CLINT.
#
# The input is the program, so a device's address is no use as bytes:
# it has to be built in a register and stored through, and an interrupt
# the store raises has to wait, masked, for an enable the translator
# declines -- or the run is set aside as asynchronous (fuzz_harness.h).
# Without the device seeds the fuzzer did not get there in 300 s
# (docs/fuzzing.md, "Mutants"). Each token is one step, as the assembly
# on the `#:` line above it, assembled by scripts/fuzz-dict.py; the
# registers are the seeds' -- t0 the address, t1 the value -- so that
# tokens dropped into one input compose. mstatus.MIE starts clear and
# mie with MSIE and MTIE set.
#
# The `#!` line is the claim that they compose: in that order they
# take a software interrupt that both backends compare, with translated
# code after the enable -- so that a dispatcher which never takes an
# interrupt disagrees (docs/fuzzing.md, mutant A). The fuzz tree's
# fuzz-rv32-jit-dict test runs it (scripts/fuzz-dict.py --compose).
#! clint_msip one_t1 store_t1 mie_on_then_add

# The CLINT's msip word, and its mtimecmp page.
#: lui t0, 0x2000
clint_msip="\xb7\x02\x00\x02"
#: lui t0, 0x2004
clint_mtimecmp="\xb7\x42\x00\x02"

# msip reads bit 0, and t1 starts even.
#: addi t1, zero, 1
one_t1="\x13\x03\x10\x00"
#: sw t1, 0(t0)
store_t1="\x23\xa0\x62\x00"
#: sw zero, 0(t0)
store_zero="\x23\xa0\x02\x00"
# mtimecmp's high word to zero puts it below mtime: MTIP.
#: sw zero, 4(t0)
store_zero_hi="\x23\xa2\x02\x00"

# The enable, and the rest of what decides whether one is taken.
# The enable with translated code after it: an interrupt the enable
# admits is taken by whichever backend runs that code, which is where
# a dispatcher's mistake shows. With only the ECALL fill after it, both
# take it in the interpreter, and a mutant of the dispatcher passes.
#: csrsi mstatus, 8 | addi a1, a1, 1
mie_on_then_add="\x73\x60\x04\x30\x93\x85\x15\x00"
#: csrsi mstatus, 8
mie_on="\x73\x60\x04\x30"
#: csrci mstatus, 8
mie_off="\x73\x70\x04\x30"
#: csrci mie, 8
msie_off="\x73\x70\x44\x30"
#: csrr a0, mip
read_mip="\x73\x25\x40\x34"
#: wfi
wfi="\x73\x00\x50\x10"
#: mret
mret="\x73\x00\x20\x30"
